    <string name="location_auto">Automatic location</string>
    <string name="location_auto_sub">Off by default. When on, a background task may read one fix if always-allow is granted. This does not add a geofence or listen all day.</string>
    <string name="location_note">Mika uses the Android location service, not a separate map vendor. A place name appears only when the system geocoder returns one. Coordinates and calendar titles are not written to the run log. Mika reads location only after you grant it. If you ask for weather without naming a city, that one request sends the coordinates to Open-Meteo and nowhere else. Naming a city does not read the phone location. Battery limits can block a background reading. Not verified on a Samsung device.</string>
